From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SDBM_File: use the typed memory release macro

GCC 14 treats incompatible pointer types as errors.  The lowercase
safefree() macro passes its argument directly to Perl_safesysfree(), whose
configured Malloc_t parameter may be char *.  SDBM_File is a structure
pointer, so this no longer compiles on such hosts.

Use Safefree(), which performs the intended Malloc_t conversion before
calling the allocator-specific release function.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
 ext/SDBM_File/SDBM_File.xs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/ext/SDBM_File/SDBM_File.xs
+++ b/ext/SDBM_File/SDBM_File.xs
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ sdbm_DESTROY(db)
 		if (db->filter[i])
 		    SvREFCNT_dec_NN(db->filter[i]);
 	    } while (i-- > 0);
-	    safefree(db) ;
+	    Safefree(db) ;
 	}
 
 datum_value
